      "rev_n_1_b98c46_0": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_1_b98c46_0",
        "node_id": "n_1_b98c46",
        "thought_text": "Calculate the total power for each possible starting task and choose the one with the minimum total power.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "root",
        "replaces_revision_id": null,
        "feedback_id": null,
        "created_at": 1794401003.382407
      },
      "rev_n_2_3485d9_0": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_2_3485d9_0",
        "node_id": "n_2_3485d9",
        "thought_text": "Notice that the tasks can be divided into groups of k consecutive tasks. Calculate the maximum power in each group and find the starting task that minimizes the sum of these maximum powers.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "root",
        "replaces_revision_id": null,
        "feedback_id": null,
        "created_at": 1794401003.382436
      },
      "rev_n_3_28ac7b_0": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_3_28ac7b_0",
        "node_id": "n_3_28ac7b",
        "thought_text": "Since the tasks repeat in a cycle of n, we can leverage this periodicity to reduce the number of calculations by considering only the first k tasks and determining the optimal shift based on their pattern.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "root",
        "replaces_revision_id": null,
        "feedback_id": null,
        "created_at": 1794401003.3824499
      },
      "rev_n_4_0dc532_0": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_4_0dc532_0",
        "node_id": "n_4_0dc532",
        "thought_text": "Calculate the cumulative power for each possible starting task and find the minimum. Since n is divisible by k, we can divide the tasks into groups of k and calculate the sum of powers for each group, then find the minimum sum.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "-2305211549909665135",
        "replaces_revision_id": null,
        "feedback_id": null,
        "created_at": 1794401357.571676
      },
      "rev_n_5_2bf814_0": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_5_2bf814_0",
        "node_id": "n_5_2bf814",
        "thought_text": "Instead of calculating the total power for each starting task individually, which could be inefficient for large n, use a sliding window approach to efficiently compute the total power for each starting task by reusing previously computed sums.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "-2305211549909665135",
        "replaces_revision_id": null,
        "feedback_id": null,
        "created_at": 1794401357.571689
      },
      "rev_n_6_c7dfa8_0": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_6_c7dfa8_0",
        "node_id": "n_6_c7dfa8",
        "thought_text": "Optimize the calculation by leveraging the periodic nature of the task sequence. Since Dima completes k-1 tasks before being told off again, we can compute the total power for the first k tasks and then adjust this sum for each subsequent starting point by removing the power of the task that is no longer included and adding the power of the new task that is included.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "-2305211549909665135",
        "replaces_revision_id": null,
        "feedback_id": null,
        "created_at": 1794401357.5716941
      },
      "rev_n_7_6a9fb9_0": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_7_6a9fb9_0",
        "node_id": "n_7_6a9fb9",
        "thought_text": "Re-evaluate the grouping of tasks. Instead of fixed groups, consider sliding windows of size k and calculate the sum of the maximum values within each window. The starting task should minimize this sum.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "1059155689622261590",
        "replaces_revision_id": null,
        "feedback_id": null,
        "created_at": 1794401494.827692
      },
      "rev_n_8_58a89e_0": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_8_58a89e_0",
        "node_id": "n_8_58a89e",
        "thought_text": "Implement a prefix sum array to efficiently calculate the sum of any subarray. This could help in determining the optimal starting task by minimizing the cumulative power of Inna's reprimands.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "1059155689622261590",
        "replaces_revision_id": null,
        "feedback_id": null,
        "created_at": 1794401494.827706
      },
      "rev_n_9_f48d37_0": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_9_f48d37_0",
        "node_id": "n_9_f48d37",
        "thought_text": "Use a binary search approach to find the optimal starting task. By comparing the total power for different starting points, binary search can help identify the minimum power configuration more efficiently.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "1059155689622261590",
        "replaces_revision_id": null,
        "feedback_id": null,
        "created_at": 1794401494.82771
      },
      "rev_n_10_a5866f_0": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_10_a5866f_0",
        "node_id": "n_10_a5866f",
        "thought_text": "Since the tasks repeat every n tasks, we can calculate the total power Dima gets told off with for each possible starting task within the first k tasks. Then, we can find the starting task that results in the minimum total power.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "4770638103775478118",
        "replaces_revision_id": null,
        "feedback_id": null,
        "created_at": 1794401624.2937138
      },
      "rev_n_11_f412bb_0": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_11_f412bb_0",
        "node_id": "n_11_f412bb",
        "thought_text": "We can optimize the calculation by recognizing that the sequence of tasks Dima completes is periodic with a period of k. Therefore, we only need to consider the impact of the tasks from 1 to k and use this pattern to determine the total power for any starting task.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "4770638103775478118",
        "replaces_revision_id": null,
        "feedback_id": null,
        "created_at": 1794401624.2937431
      },
      "rev_n_12_fa4cf4_0": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_12_fa4cf4_0",
        "node_id": "n_12_fa4cf4",
        "thought_text": "Instead of calculating the total power for each starting task individually, we can sort the tasks by their power and determine the optimal starting task based on the sorted order. This approach minimizes the total power by prioritizing tasks with lower power values.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "4770638103775478118",
